   "source": [
    "**Your answer:** Since these are partial derivatives, we are only conserned about how y grows in this case with respect to y and b. The expression for y is wx+b, meaning that the change in value of w is amplified by the value of x. Therefore as for example w inrease by 1.0, it will cause y to increase by x*1.0. We therefore need to know the value of x to determine the derivative of y. In the case of calculating dy_db, b is an independent term in y = wx+b, so we don't need to know the value of any other term to find the derivative of y. "
   ]
