   },
   "source": [
    "**Your answer:** Increasing the step size would reduce the error more rapidly, at least in the first steps. But it would also increase the risk of making parameter changes too large to accurately estimate the true value. Kind of like hitting a golf ball past the hole with too much speed, resulting in the ball to roll too far past the hole each attempt. Decreasing the step size too much would make the estimations converge slower, and it might require more iterations to reach an accurate estimation. "
   ]
