     "solution": true,
     "task": false
    }
   },
   "source": [
    "**Your answer:** One important difference is that the outputs when using a sigmoid function does not need to sum to 1, whereas the outputs from using the softmax function allways sum to 1. So when the learning algorithm needs to choose between one of the possible datapoints, the sigmoid function will point on only one of those classes by outputting the highest number. This also means that one output will have have an effect on the other outputs. When using the sigmoid function, there can be multiple high value outputs. "
   ]
